{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548196-poll-what-kind-of-storyteller-toolkit-would-you-want-most","id":1548196,"title":"POLL: What kind of storyteller toolkit would you want most?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-04T11:40:55-08:00","id":1548196,"title":"POLL: What kind of storyteller toolkit would you want most?","content":"I love Mage: the Ascension, and I want to give back to the game and the community. It does have a bit of a reputation of being scary to run, and I'd love to help others over those bumps.<br /> <br /> <b>If someone with a lot of comfort and experience running Mage were to put up a short, focused guide, which one of these three things would be most interesting or helpful to you?</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Rules</b>: Tips to adjudicate magick rolls consistently, tie mechanics and stories closer together</li> <li><b>Stories</b>: Turn classic plot and character archetypes into Mage stories, pacing for different length sessions/campaigns</li> <li><b>Campaign</b>: A set of connected stories ready to run, out of the box</li> </ol>Thanks folks! I'd love to eventually help with all the things, but best to start small, with the things you think will do you the most good.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28726-faust79","name":"faust79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T07:14:25-08:00","id":1548222,"title":"","content":"For interest, I think stories would be the best especially if it breaks down different story types and themes and good reasons to interact with different parts of the world. Things like where might individual cabals of Traditions and Technocracy mages come into conflict, even if they aren't looking for each other? What are good reasons to go into the Umbra? How to jump from normalcy to strangeness and back again? Etc.<br /> <br /> For helpfulness, the rules for magic in M20 are spotty and inconsistent, so a clear and simple guide would help everyone. However, that's more of a rewrite than a guide, since you have to actually decide things M20 didn't, like what rank do you need for a locking sphere (M20 doesn't say, but always uses rank 2, HDYDT says transmutation level but constantly contradicts itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}